---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: The required check nextcloud
    accDescr: A pull request or a push to main that changes no file the end-to-end tests cover passes the check nextcloud in seconds, with a notice. Otherwise, and in the weekly run and a run started by hand, run-all.sh tests every Nextcloud version from min-version to max-version at the same time in one job, and beside them upgrade.sh upgrades the last release to the checkout, on the newest version in a pull request and on every version elsewhere; the check passes only when every version and every upgrade passes, and the log of each is a group of its own. When the weekly run or a run started by hand on main fails, the job issue about the supported Nextcloud opens the issue A supported Nextcloud release breaks the app with the versions that broke, or adds the run to it; when such a run passes, it closes the issue. A pull request or a push never touches the issue.

    change["Pull request<br>or push to main"]
    timed["Weekly run<br>or a start by hand"]
    scope{"A file the tests<br>cover changed?"}
    skipped["nextcloud passes in seconds<br>with a notice"]
    all["run-all.sh<br>one download of the browser"]
    low["`Nextcloud *min-version*`"]
    middle["every version<br>in between"]
    high["`Nextcloud *max-version*`"]
    upgrade["upgrade.sh: from the last release<br>newest version on a pull request,<br>every version elsewhere"]
    every{"Every version and<br>every upgrade passes?"}
    passed["nextcloud passes"]
    failed["nextcloud fails<br>the log of each version<br>in a group of its own"]
    opened["opens the issue<br>A supported Nextcloud<br>release breaks the app<br>or adds the run to it,<br>with the versions that broke"]
    closed["closes the issue<br>if it is open"]

    change --> scope
    scope -- "no" --> skipped
    scope -- "yes" --> all
    timed --> all
    all --> low & middle & high & upgrade --> every
    every -- "yes" --> passed
    every -- "no" --> failed
    failed -- "weekly run or<br>by hand on main" --> opened
    passed -- "weekly run or<br>by hand on main" --> closed

    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef fail fill:#dc26262e,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
    class change person
    class timed,all,low,middle,high,upgrade,opened bot
    class skipped,passed,closed done
    class failed fail
